// Title: Windows Credential Guard Related Registry Value Deleted - Registry
// Sigma ID: d645ef86-2396-48a1-a2b6-b629ca3f57ff
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2025-12-26 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects attempts to disable Windows Credential Guard by deleting registry values. Credential
//   Guard uses virtualization-based security to isolate secrets so that only privileged system
//   software can access them. Adversaries may disable Credential Guard to gain access to sensitive
//   credentials stored in the system, such as NTLM hashes and Kerberos tickets, which can be used
//   for lateral movement and privilege escalation.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20260215021829/https://github.com/DambergC/SaveFolder/blob/90e945eba80fae85f2d54b4616e05a44ec90c500/Cygate%20Installation%20tool%206.22/Script/OSD/OSDeployment-CredentialGuardDisable.ps1#L50
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/identity-protection/credential-guard/configure
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cb982537eb7397f93785ec066cce7b017050a43f/rules/windows/registry/registry_delete/registry_delete_disable_credential_guard.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (ActionType in~ ("RegistryKeyDeleted", "RegistryValueDeleted")) and (RegistryKey endswith "\\DeviceGuard\\EnableVirtualizationBasedSecurity" or RegistryKey endswith "\\DeviceGuard\\LsaCfgFlags" or RegistryKey endswith "\\DeviceGuard\\RequirePlatformSecurityFeatures" or RegistryKey endswith "\\Lsa\\LsaCfgFlags")
